(4230966, 606826, 79657, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Ursula. We should go to Jasper together next year *winks*. Sure Medicine Lake is always photogenic no matter when and where we took the picture from but your shots are even more amazing.<br/>My trip included 2300 km of driving, visiting 6 lakes, taking 1000+ pictures and climbing a glacier in a total of 4 days.<br/> <br/>Cheers,</td>', 'Congratulations Ursula. We should go to Jasper together next year *winks*. Sure Medicine Lake is always photogenic no matter when and where we took the picture from but your shots are even more amazing.My trip included 2300 km of driving, visiting 6 lakes, taking 1000+ pictures and climbing a glacier in a total of 4 days. Cheers,', '2007-11-08 01:34:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4230973, 605712, 69325, '<td valign="top">beautiful colors and detail on this. you are really hotting a stride these days, congrats on the top ten my friend. I think maybe you are going to rack up a few ribbons in the weeks and months ahead! i love floral shots and im gonna fav this one...LOVE it</td>', 'beautiful colors and detail on this. you are really hotting a stride these days, congrats on the top ten my friend. I think maybe you are going to rack up a few ribbons in the weeks and months ahead! i love floral shots and im gonna fav this one...LOVE it', '2007-11-08 01:38:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231142, 606826, 48424, '<td valign="top">Thanks for posting the originals Ursula. I was expecting more heavy processing but apart from the dodge/burn on "apocalyptic vision", there''s not much more than what a tinted filter would have achieved. I''m even more impressed, if that''s possible! :) The originals are stand out pictures in their own right, I love the dark exposure, gives them more of a "fantasy" feel.</td>', 'Thanks for posting the originals Ursula. I was expecting more heavy processing but apart from the dodge/burn on "apocalyptic vision", there''s not much more than what a tinted filter would have achieved. I''m even more impressed, if that''s possible! :) The originals are stand out pictures in their own right, I love the dark exposure, gives them more of a "fantasy" feel.', '2007-11-08 03:47:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231174, 606418, 28742, '<td valign="top">Great photo, Deb! It is interesting, exotic (from a US perspective) and has all the technicals. Probably lacks the right challenge - it definitely fits, but might do better in "construction" or something. Lacks that WOW factor as well - not sure what you can do about that.<br/> <br/>I would name it "Rebuilding the Tower of Babel" just because that''s the first thing I thought of. :)</td>', 'Great photo, Deb! It is interesting, exotic (from a US perspective) and has all the technicals. Probably lacks the right challenge - it definitely fits, but might do better in "construction" or something. Lacks that WOW factor as well - not sure what you can do about that. I would name it "Rebuilding the Tower of Babel" just because that''s the first thing I thought of. :)', '2007-11-08 04:35:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231548, 606456, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh!  He does look ever so slightly like The Donald, doesn''t he?  From a technical standpoint, he''s a bit unfocused (though moving kids are darn hard to shoot, especially at 1/30th of a second) and that white thing is distracting, though I very much like your rationale on that.  :-)  The rest of the background doesn''t bother me at all - I like it as atmosphere and setting.</td>', 'Heh!  He does look ever so slightly like The Donald, doesn''t he?  From a technical standpoint, he''s a bit unfocused (though moving kids are darn hard to shoot, especially at 1/30th of a second) and that white thing is distracting, though I very much like your rationale on that.  :-)  The rest of the background doesn''t bother me at all - I like it as atmosphere and setting.', '2007-11-08 09:00:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231560, 606584, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like this and find it better than the "snapshot" we''ve been discussing.  The angle is what changes it from a simple snapshot.  I''ve not seen a pack of Segways before so I found this to be quite intriguing.  Sometimes it''s just fun to post things that others might find interesting (we hope) - see my entry next to yours on the Suck results page for something similar.  :-)</td>', 'I like this and find it better than the "snapshot" we''ve been discussing.  The angle is what changes it from a simple snapshot.  I''ve not seen a pack of Segways before so I found this to be quite intriguing.  Sometimes it''s just fun to post things that others might find interesting (we hope) - see my entry next to yours on the Suck results page for something similar.  :-)', '2007-11-08 09:04:43.000000', NULL, 0),
