(4234032, 605712, 68035, '<td valign="top">Blimey Rozter....5 challenges 3 stars and one ribbon!!!!!!!!<br/> <br/>I love the graduated peach backdrop on the shot which really sets the flower off nicely<br/> <br/>The dof is so cool as well and it is brilliant the way the sharpness in the foreground dissolves slightly and then seems to return on parts of the flower in the background, before returning to bokeh<br/> <br/>Cooool trick<br/> <br/></td>', 'Blimey Rozter....5 challenges 3 stars and one ribbon!!!!!!!! I love the graduated peach backdrop on the shot which really sets the flower off nicely The dof is so cool as well and it is brilliant the way the sharpness in the foreground dissolves slightly and then seems to return on parts of the flower in the background, before returning to bokeh Cooool trick ', '2007-11-09 05:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4234452, 606725, 24454, '<td valign="top">I don''t think it''s a shoehorn at all :)  New York is "something" New.   And what a fabulous, very deserving photo to win top honors.  I love your angle.   It makes it so interesting!  Congratulations!!!!!</td>', 'I don''t think it''s a shoehorn at all :)  New York is "something" New.   And what a fabulous, very deserving photo to win top honors.  I love your angle.   It makes it so interesting!  Congratulations!!!!!', '2007-11-09 10:33:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4234855, 606418, 66952, '<td valign="top">Hi Deb,<br/> <br/>I think this is actually a much better than average photo, entered in the wrong challenge. It doesn''t really say "new" to my American brain. <br/> <br/>As far as the image goes, since you couldn''t take it at a different time of day, I think you could get a lot by using levels to make the midtones (a lot) darker. the image isn''t really overexposed, the highlights and shadows are in the right place, but overall, the image is too bright. <br/> <br/>The other thing would be cropping off the bottom "empty" portion. It isn''t really adding anything to the shot, and just sucking my attention away from the important bits.</td>', 'Hi Deb, I think this is actually a much better than average photo, entered in the wrong challenge. It doesn''t really say "new" to my American brain.  As far as the image goes, since you couldn''t take it at a different time of day, I think you could get a lot by using levels to make the midtones (a lot) darker. the image isn''t really overexposed, the highlights and shadows are in the right place, but overall, the image is too bright.  The other thing would be cropping off the bottom "empty" portion. It isn''t really adding anything to the shot, and just sucking my attention away from the important bits.', '2007-11-09 13:32:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4235013, 606826, 5112, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Meoux:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations Ursula. We should go to Jasper together next year *winks*. Sure Medicine Lake is always photogenic no matter when and where we took the picture from but your shots are even more amazing.<br/>My trip included 2300 km of driving, visiting 6 lakes, taking 1000+ pictures and climbing a glacier in a total of 4 days.<br/> <br/>Cheers, </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ooohhh, that would be fun!  :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Meoux: Congratulations Ursula. We should go to Jasper together next year *winks*. Sure Medicine Lake is always photogenic no matter when and where we took the picture from but your shots are even more amazing.My trip included 2300 km of driving, visiting 6 lakes, taking 1000+ pictures and climbing a glacier in a total of 4 days. Cheers,   Ooohhh, that would be fun!  :)', '2007-11-09 14:55:53.000000', NULL, 0),
